1
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:02,530
A little further to the right, Tom.

2
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:03,530
Is this OK?

3
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:05,530
Good. What do you think, Richard?

4
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:06,530
I like it there.

5
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:09,530
It's the first thing people will see when they come in.

6
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:11,530
It sets the tone for the whole show.

7
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:13,530
The next thing they'll see is

8
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:16,530
this enlargement with the words Family Album, U.S.A. Family Album, U.S.A.

9
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:19,530
I can't believe this is really happening!

10
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:20,530
You've earned it.

11
00:02:20,530 --> 00:02:22,530
Years of work went into these pictures.

12
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:25,530
I know, but it's still a dream come true.

13
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:26,530
Well, remember,

14
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:27,530
we're not sure

15
00:02:27,530 --> 00:02:29,530
what the critics are going to write about your show yet.

16
00:02:29,530 --> 00:02:31,530
And you never know

17
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:34,530
what the man from the New York Times is going to say about it.

18
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:35,530
Are you worried?

19
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:36,530
I always worry.

20
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:38,530
The reviews of this show

21
00:02:38,530 --> 00:02:40,530
are important for the sales of your book.

22
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:42,530
When do we see the reviews?

23
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:43,530
Soon.

24
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:45,530
One of the critics is coming over this morning for a preview.

25
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:47,530
I hope he's in a good mood.

26
00:02:47,530 --> 00:02:48,530
So do I.

27
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:53,530
Marilyn and I hope to use money from the sales of this book Marilyn

28
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:54,530
to buy a new house.

29
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:56,530
The book will be a success.

30
00:02:56,530 --> 00:02:57,530
And the show will help promote it.

31
00:02:57,530 --> 00:03:01,530
Speaking of promoting the book,

32
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:02,530
do I really have to

33
00:03:02,530 --> 00:03:05,530
autograph copies for the guests at the opening?

34
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:06,530
It's common practice.

35
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:09,530
I feel uncomfortable about it.

36
00:03:09,530 --> 00:03:11,530
A lot of people come to openings

37
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:12,530
just so they can get

38
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:15,530
the autograph of somebody who may be famous someday.

39
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:17,530
Couldn't we wait until I'm famous?

40
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:19,530
That might be sooner than you think.

41
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:21,530
This one over here, Mr. Carlson?

42
00:03:21,530 --> 00:03:24,530
A little further back, Tom.

43
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:25,530
It's too close to the refreshments.

44
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:28,530
No, I think this one belongs in the "people-at-work" section.

45
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:31,530
You may be right.

46
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:32,530
Try it there, Tom.

47
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:33,530
Right.

48
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:36,530
Nervous about the opening tonight?

49
00:03:36,530 --> 00:03:37,530
Nervous?

50
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:41,530
No. I'm scared to death.

51
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:42,530
How about guests?

52
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:44,530
How many people will you be bringing?

53
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:47,530
Well, my family, I guess.

54
00:03:47,530 --> 00:03:50,530
My wife Marilyn, my father and mother,

55
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:52,530
my brother Robbie,

56
00:03:52,530 --> 00:03:54,530
my sister and her husband and their daughter.

57
00:03:54,530 --> 00:03:55,530
And my grandfather.

58
00:03:55,530 --> 00:03:57,530
Is that too many?

59
00:03:57,530 --> 00:03:59,530
No such thing as "too many" at an opening.

60
00:03:59,530 --> 00:04:01,530
I hope they like it.

61
00:04:01,530 --> 00:04:04,530
Your family or the public?

62
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:06,530
Everybody.

63
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,530
But especially my family.

64
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:10,530
They've stood by me through all this.

65
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:11,530
I'm sure they'll like it.

66
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:14,530
Harvey, how are you? Harvey

67
00:04:14,530 --> 00:04:16,530
Mitchell, so nice of you to come. Mitchell

68
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:18,530
Richard, this is Mitchell Johnson. Richard

69
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:20,530
Mitchell is

70
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:22,530
one of the most important syndicated reviewers in the country.

71
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:25,530
Well, you're the young man who did all this.

72
00:04:25,530 --> 00:04:27,530
I'm afraid so.

73
00:04:27,530 --> 00:04:28,530
Nice to meet you.

74
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:29,530
Nice to meet you, Mr. Johnson.

75
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:32,530
Mitchell has always encouraged new talent. Mitchell

76
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:34,530
Well ... you mind if I look around

77
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:35,530
and see what it says to me?

78
00:04:35,530 --> 00:05:28,530
Be our guest.

79
00:05:28,530 --> 00:05:33,530
Mm-hmm, hmm, uh-huh.

80
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:40,530
What does that mean when he goes,

81
00:05:40,530 --> 00:05:42,530
"Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, mm-hmm"?

82
00:05:42,530 --> 00:05:45,530
It probably means he's clearing his throat.

83
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:46,530
I don't know.

84
00:05:46,530 --> 00:05:49,530
I don't care what the critics say, Mr. Stewart.

85
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:50,530
Your work is brilliant.

86
00:05:50,530 --> 00:05:51,530
Thank you, Tom.

87
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:54,530
Tom is studying photography at NYU. Tom

88
00:05:54,530 --> 00:05:57,530
He's working with me during the summer months as an intern.

89
00:05:57,530 --> 00:06:00,530
Oh, really?

90
00:05:57,530 --> 00:05:59,530
I'd like to see your work.

91
00:05:59,530 --> 00:06:00,530
It's not good enough to show.

92
00:06:00,530 --> 00:06:01,530
I'm still learning.

93
00:06:01,530 --> 00:06:02,530
Oh, I'd still like to see your work.

94
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:04,530
You may be the next Ansel Adams and not even know it.

95
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:05,530
If you really mean it,

96
00:06:05,530 --> 00:06:07,530
I'll bring some of my pictures into the gallery.

97
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:08,530
I do mean it.

98
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:12,530
Very interesting pictures, Mr. Stewart.

99
00:06:12,530 --> 00:06:14,530
You have a most unusual eye.

100
00:06:14,530 --> 00:06:15,530
Thank you.

101
00:06:15,530 --> 00:06:17,530
I hope that's a compliment.

102
00:06:17,530 --> 00:06:18,530
It is.

103
00:06:18,530 --> 00:06:20,530
Are you going to be reviewing the show, Mitchell?

104
00:06:20,530 --> 00:06:22,530
Oh, yes. It's definitely worth reviewing.

105
00:06:22,530 --> 00:06:24,530
Favorably?

106
00:06:24,530 --> 00:06:26,530
Oh, you know I never answer that question, Harvey.

107
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:28,530
I'd like an advance copy of the book, though,

108
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:29,530
so I can study it.

109
00:06:29,530 --> 00:06:32,530
I have an autographed one in my office.

110
00:06:32,530 --> 00:06:36,530
Tom, would you give Mr. Johnson Tom

111
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:37,530
the copy of Richard's book on my desk?

112
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:38,530
Just follow me, Mr. Johnson.

113
00:06:38,530 --> 00:06:39,530
Sure.

114
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:44,530
Do you think he liked my photographs?

115
00:06:44,530 --> 00:06:46,530
We'll know when tonight's papers come out.

116
00:06:46,530 --> 00:06:49,530
Keep your fingers crossed.
